{"id":"19d430bc-1f7b-4d6c-b054-7aea530f75f4","fragment":{"type":"general","created_at":"2025-12-16T19:21:49.877Z","entry_text":"Cael, Rynn and multiple shifter children have been captured by slavers in a nearby camp.","updated_at":"2025-12-16T19:21:49.877Z","display_name":"Captured Allies"},"embedding":null,"created_at":"2025-12-16T19:21:49.864749+00:00","updated_at":"2025-12-16T19:21:49.864749+00:00","world_id":"b3de4b0a-a879-43cf-8256-2153a5ff97a9","visibility":"private","owner_user_id":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000a001","is_official":false,"keywords":["Cael","Rynn","captured","slavers","objective"],"entity_id":null,"story_id":null},
{"id":"42f75059-64c0-490f-b77c-db3e80bfd337","fragment":{"type":"backstory","created_at":"2025-12-15T17:41:04.176Z","entry_text":"I didn't learn to walk between worlds; I fell. It happened during the Eclipse of Three Suns in my homeworld. One moment I was running from the Guard, the next, the cobblestones turned to mist beneath my boots. I fell through the geometry of the universe for what felt like an eternity, eventually landing here—bruised, confused, and smelling of ozone. Now, I don't just see walls; I see suggestions.","updated_at":"2025-12-15T17:41:04.176Z","display_name":"The First Fracture"},"embedding":null,"created_at":"2025-12-15T17:41:04.182038+00:00","updated_at":"2025-12-15T17:41:04.182038+00:00","world_id":"b3de4b0a-a879-43cf-8256-2153a5ff97a9","visibility":"private","owner_user_id":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000a001","is_official":false,"keywords":["origin","inciting-incident","dimension-hop","homeworld"],"entity_id":null,"story_id":null},
{"id":"abbc0ec5-7459-47d0-81d5-03482b1b127f","fragment":{"type":"backstory","created_at":"2025-12-15T17:42:06.122Z","entry_text":"Drifting isn't free. Every time I step through a rift, a little bit of me stays behind in the grey space. If I jump too many times in one day, the colors of the real world start to fade, and I can hear them scratching at the edges of my perception. I have to anchor myself with heavy food and strong drink to remind my body it still exists in three dimensions.","updated_at":"2025-12-15T17:42:06.122Z","display_name":"Void Sickness"},"embedding":null,"created_at":"2025-12-15T17:42:06.13599+00:00","updated_at":"2025-12-15T17:42:06.13599+00:00","world_id":"b3de4b0a-a879-43cf-8256-2153a5ff97a9","visibility":"private","owner_user_id":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000a001","is_official":false,"keywords":["weakness","cost","void","sickness","limit"],"entity_id":null,"story_id":null},
{"id":"d7c92772-2929-4d56-9823-3e27adde7c28","fragment":{"type":"backstory","created_at":"2025-12-15T17:50:04.914Z","entry_text":"This brass compass doesn't point North. It points to the nearest \"High Reality\" zone—places where the fabric of the world is thickest and most stable. I use it to find safe places to sleep. If the needle starts spinning wildly, I know a Rift Storm is coming, or worse... a Reality Eater is nearby.","updated_at":"2025-12-15T17:50:04.914Z","display_name":"The Anchor Compass"},"embedding":null,"created_at":"2025-12-15T17:50:04.945314+00:00","updated_at":"2025-12-15T17:50:04.945314+00:00","world_id":"b3de4b0a-a879-43cf-8256-2153a5ff97a9","visibility":"private","owner_user_id":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000a001","is_official":false,"keywords":["gear","navigation","artifact","compass","tool"],"entity_id":null,"story_id":null}
]$seed$::jsonb)
